regexec.c, oniguruma.h: the regset search caches forward_search per regex

onig_regset_search in ONIG_REGSET_POSITION_LEAD mode calls forward_search
for each regex to find its next candidate position. The port searches the
same line many times, from later and later positions, so most of these
calls repeat work. With this patch, onig_regset_search_keyed takes a
non-zero key that names an immutable string; within the same key, str and
end, the set keeps, for each regex, the position forward_search started
from and the candidate it found (or none). forward_search returns the
leftmost candidate, so the result holds for any start between the two, and
"none" holds for any later start. The cache is used only for UTF-8 with
range == end, and not when start, or the first byte of an exact string,
is a UTF-8 continuation byte. onig_regset_add and onig_regset_replace
reset it. Defining ONIG_REGSET_FS_VERIFY checks every cache hit against a
real forward_search and aborts on a difference.

See rust/vendor/README.md.

